# Test and coverage output
#
# Unanchored on purpose: `go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...` run from a
# subdirectory writes the file there, and a leading slash would have matched
# only a copy at the repository root while every other one showed up as an
# untracked file.
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Compiled test binaries and profiles. `go test -c` and the -cpuprofile /
# -memprofile flags drop these next to the package under test, so these are
# unanchored too.
*.test
*.prof
cpu.out
mem.out
block.out
mutex.out
trace.out

# Build output
/dist/

# The non-wasm stub main of the demo builds a host binary of this name when it
# is compiled without GOOS=js; it is a build artifact, never a checked-in file.
/examples/wasm-demo/wasm-demo

# Frontend tooling for the web demo
node_modules/

# Agent worktrees
.claude/

# Trunk's configuration, local cache and generated state. Nothing under it is
# tracked — the CLI set this repository up in single-player mode — and it was
# hidden only by .git/info/exclude, which lives in one clone and is never
# pushed, so everyone else saw the whole tree as untracked.
.trunk/

# Editor and IDE state. Per-developer, never part of the build.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
